          "filename": "Oradour-sur-Glane-Sign-1428.jpg",
          "caption": "A sign in the cemetery of Oradour-sur-Glane.\nThis small sign reads \"Crimes committed by the 2nd SS Division \"Das Reich\" on the orders of General Lammerding\". I am however not sure this information is correct; according to the wikipedia article, it was the Waffen-SS \"Der Führer\" regiment who was responsible. (in fact the Waffen-SS \"Der Führer\" regiment was a part of the 2nd SS Division \"Das Reich\")\n\nThis is a photograph which I took during a visit to the French village Oradour-sur-Glane on June 11 2004, exactly 60 years after its destruction by the German army during World War II.",
          "alt": "A sign in the cemetery of Oradour-sur-Glane.\nThis small sign reads \"Crimes committed by the 2nd SS Division \"Das Reich\" on the orders of General Lammerding\". I am however not sure this information is correct; according to the wikipedia article, it was the Waffen-SS \"Der Führer\" regiment who was responsible. (in fact the Waffen-SS \"Der Führer\" regiment was a part of the 2nd SS Division \"Das Reich\")\n\nThis is a photograph which I took during a visit to the French village Oradour-sur-Glane on June 11 2004, exactly 60 years after its destruction by the German army during World War II.",
